          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/924f4c4ac78b0cd3b917c694f42c0651a6f3003a",
          "sha": "924f4c4ac78b0cd3b917c694f42c0651a6f3003a",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/924f4c4ac78b0cd3b917c694f42c0651a6f3003a"
        }
      ],
      "message": "net: skip unusable addrman picks in ThreadPrivateBroadcast\n\nWhen a transaction is privately broadcast, ThreadPrivateBroadcast keeps\nopening connections until all planned sends are done. If every address\naddrman returns for the picked network is one we already have a\nconnection to (or is banned/discouraged), OpenNetworkConnection() fails\nimmediately and the loop retries every 100ms, logging a \"Failed to\nconnect ... will retry\" line each time. On a node that only knows a few\nonion/I2P peers this spins for as long as the sends remain pending,\nwhich can be indefinitely.\n\nCheck the conditions that make OpenNetworkConnection() refuse an address\nbefore attempting the connection and treat such picks like invalid ones:\nretry after 500ms once this has happened 100 times in a row, and log\nabout it once per 100 picks instead of on every attempt.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Kevin Ravensberg",
        "email": "kevinravensberg@proton.me",
        "date": "2026-10-17T17:54:37Z"
      },
